  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nDrier air begins advecting into the region today as winds shift\nout of the north. Additional rounds of scattered showers and\nthunderstorms will be possible along the leading edge of the \nmoisture gradient as it pushes south through the area, with the\nhighest rain chances located along and south of I-70. Cooler\nsurface temperatures and weaker lapse rates aloft continue to\nlimit instability, so the severe threat remains low except\nperhaps an off-chance for a few strong wind gusts south of the\nMason-Dixon Line. The onset of northerly flow then ushers drier\nair and seasonable temperatures Sunday into early next week.",
